## Implementation Plan: Convert datum Workflow Dashboard from Custom CSS to Tailwind + Chart.js

### 1. CDN Script Tags to Add

Replace the `<head>` section (lines 273-437) with the following structure. Add three CDN script tags before the closing `</head>`:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
<script>
tailwind.config = {
  darkMode: 'class',
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        bg: '#0a0a0f',
        'bg-card': '#12121a',
        'bg-hover': '#1a1a28',
        'bg-phase': '#0e0e16',
        'bg-expand': '#161622',
        border: '#2a2a3a',
        dim: '#707080',
        bright: '#f0f0ff',
        accent: '#6c8cff',
        green: '#4cda8c',
        yellow: '#e8c94a',
        red: '#e84a5a',
        orange: '#e89a4a',
        purple: '#a06cff',
      },
      fontFamily: {
        mono: ["'SF Mono'", "'Cascadia Code'", "'JetBrains Mono'", 'monospace'],
        sans: ["'Inter'", '-apple-system', 'system-ui', 'sans-serif'],
      },
      borderRadius: {
        DEFAULT: '8px',
        sm: '4px',
      },
    },
  },
}
</script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.7/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chartjs-plugin-annotation@3.1.0/dist/chartjs-plugin-annotation.min.js"></script>
```

**CDN version pinning rationale:**
- Tailwind Play CDN: no version pin needed (always latest, non-breaking for utility classes)
- Chart.js 4.4.7: latest stable 4.x at time of writing
- chartjs-plugin-annotation 3.1.0: compatible with Chart.js 4.x

### 2. CSS That Must Be Kept (Cannot Be Expressed in Tailwind Utilities)

Create a minimal `<style>` block containing only what Tailwind cannot do:

```css
<style>
/* grid-template-rows 0fr/1fr transition for expand/collapse */
.agent-expand {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: 0fr;
  transition: grid-template-rows 0.25s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
}
.agent-expand[data-open] {
  grid-template-rows: 1fr;
}
.agent-expand > .agent-detail {
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Keyframe animations */
@keyframes pulse { 0%, 100% { opacity: 1; } 50% { opacity: 0.4; } }
@keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }

/* Spinner component */
.spinner {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border: 2px solid #4cda8c;
  border-top-color: transparent;
  border-radius: 50%;
  animation: spin 0.8s linear infinite;
}

/* Phase dot pulse for running status */
[data-status="running"] .phase-dot { animation: pulse 1.5s infinite; }

/* Scrollbar styling (optional, keep if desired) */
</style>
```

**Why these stay in CSS:**
- `grid-template-rows: 0fr/1fr` transition is a state-toggle tied to `[data-open]`. Tailwind has no `data-open:` variant by default, and even if you added one, the 0fr/1fr pattern with child `overflow: hidden` is not expressible as utilities.
- The `@keyframes` for `pulse` and `spin` require custom animation definitions. Tailwind's built-in `animate-pulse` uses opacity 0/1 (not 0.4), and `animate-spin` works but the spinner has custom sizing (8px with 2px border) that is more readable as a component class.

### 3. Complete CSS-to-Tailwind Class Mapping

Below is every CSS selector from the original `@layer` blocks, mapped to the Tailwind classes that replace it. Where a class is referenced by JS (via `querySelector`, `toggleAttribute`, or `classList`), I note whether the selector must be preserved as a data attribute or can be converted.

#### 3.1 Body & Shell (Layout layer)

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `body { font-family: var(--font-sans); background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.5; }` | `<body class="font-sans bg-bg text-[#e0e0e8] leading-normal min-h-dvh">` |
| `.shell { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 320px 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; min-height: 100dvh; }` | `<div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto p-6 grid grid-cols-[320px_1fr] gap-6 min-h-dvh max-[900px]:grid-cols-1">` |
| `header { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }` | `<header class="col-span-full flex items-baseline gap-4 flex-wrap">` |
| `header h1` | `<h1 class="font-mono text-[1.1rem] font-semibold text-bright">` |
| `.meta` | Use inline: `text-xs text-dim font-mono` |

#### 3.2 Sidebar

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.sidebar` | `<div class="flex flex-col gap-2 overflow-y-auto max-h-[calc(100dvh-5rem)]">` |
| `.filters` | `<div class="flex gap-1 mb-2 flex-wrap">` |
| `.filter-btn` | `<button class="font-mono text-[0.65rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full border border-border bg-transparent text-dim cursor-pointer transition-all duration-150 uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold hover:border-accent hover:text-[#e0e0e8]">` |
| `.filter-btn[data-active]` | Add conditional classes in JS: when active, add `border-accent bg-accent/15 text-accent`, remove `text-dim` |
| `.filter-btn .count` | `<span class="opacity-60 ml-0.5">` |

#### 3.3 Run Cards

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.run-card` | `<div class="bg-bg-card border border-border rounded px-4 py-3 cursor-pointer transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-accent hover:bg-bg-hover">` |
| `.run-card[data-selected]` | Add in JS when selected: `border-accent bg-bg-hover` |
| `.run-card[hidden]` | Keep `hidden` attribute (Tailwind respects native `hidden`) |
| `.run-name` | `<div class="font-mono text-[0.85rem] text-bright font-medium">` |
| `.run-id` | `<div class="text-[0.65rem] text-dim font-mono mt-0.5">` |
| `.run-meta` | `<div class="flex gap-3 mt-1.5 text-[0.7rem] font-mono text-dim">` |

#### 3.4 Detail View

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.detail` | `<div class="overflow-y-auto max-h-[calc(100dvh-5rem)]">` |
| `.summary-bar` | `<div class="flex gap-6 px-4 py-3 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded font-mono text-[0.8rem] mb-4 flex-wrap">` |
| `.summary-bar dt` | `<dt class="text-dim text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-widest">` |
| `.summary-bar dd` | `<dd class="text-bright font-semibold text-base">` |

#### 3.5 Phase Groups

