#### 3.6 Agent Rows

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.agent-row` | `<div class="grid grid-cols-[2fr_80px_70px_60px_3fr] gap-2 items-center px-3 py-2 border-l-[3px] border-l-transparent ml-2 text-[0.75rem] font-mono transition-colors duration-150 cursor-pointer hover:border-l-accent hover:bg-bg-hover">` |
| `.agent-row[data-state="running"]` | In JS, replace `border-l-transparent` with `border-l-green` |
| `.agent-row[data-state="queued"]` | In JS, replace `border-l-transparent` with `border-l-yellow` |
| `.agent-row[data-state="done"]` | In JS, replace `border-l-transparent` with `border-l-border` |
| `.agent-label` | `text-bright font-medium` |
| `.agent-model` | `text-dim text-[0.65rem]` |
| `.agent-tokens` | `text-dim text-right text-[0.7rem]` |
| `.agent-duration` | `text-dim text-right text-[0.7rem]` |
| `.agent-activity` | `text-dim text-[0.68rem] overflow-hidden text-ellipsis whitespace-nowrap` |

#### 3.7 Agent Expand/Detail (Hybrid: CSS + Tailwind)

The `.agent-expand` and `.agent-detail` containers keep the CSS classes from section 2 above for the `grid-template-rows` animation. Inner content uses Tailwind:

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.agent-detail` (inner) | `<div class="agent-detail px-3 bg-bg-expand border-l-[3px] border-l-accent font-mono text-[0.7rem] transition-[padding] duration-[250ms]">` |
| `.agent-expand[data-open] .agent-detail` padding | Handled in CSS (padding toggled via transition) |
| `.agent-detail .section` | `<div class="mb-2">` |
| `.agent-detail .section-title` | `<div class="text-accent text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-wide mb-0.5">` |
| `.agent-detail .section-body` | `<div class="text-dim whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-relaxed max-h-[150px] overflow-y-auto">` |
| `.agent-detail .kv` | `<div class="flex gap-4 flex-wrap">` |
| `.agent-detail .kv span` | `text-dim` |
| `.agent-detail .kv strong` | `text-bright font-medium` |

#### 3.8 Badges

Badges use `color-mix()` which Tailwind can express using the opacity modifier syntax:

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.badge` (base) | `inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[0.6rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider` |
| `.badge--running` | `bg-green/15 text-green` |
| `.badge--queued` | `bg-yellow/15 text-yellow` |
| `.badge--done` | `bg-dim/10 text-dim` |
| `.badge--completed` | `bg-green/15 text-green` |
| `.badge--failed` | `bg-red/15 text-red` |

Update the `statusBadge()` JS function to emit Tailwind classes:
```js
function statusBadge(st) {
  const styles = {
    running: 'bg-green/15 text-green',
    completed: 'bg-green/15 text-green',
    failed: 'bg-red/15 text-red',
    queued: 'bg-yellow/15 text-yellow',
  };
  const cls = styles[st] || 'bg-dim/10 text-dim';
  return `<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[0.6rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider ${cls}">${st}</span>`;
}
```

#### 3.9 Logs

| Original CSS | Tailwind Replacement |
