#### 6.2 `setFilter()` — update class toggling

```js
function setFilter(f) {
  activeFilter = f;
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(b => {
    const isActive = b.dataset.filter === f;
    b.classList.toggle('border-accent', isActive);
    b.classList.toggle('bg-accent/15', isActive);
    b.classList.toggle('text-accent', isActive);
    b.classList.toggle('border-border', !isActive);
    b.classList.toggle('text-dim', !isActive);
  });
  // Hidden logic unchanged
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-status]').forEach(c => {
    if (!c.dataset.path) return;
    c.hidden = f !== 'all' && c.dataset.status !== f;
  });
}
```

**Important note about Tailwind classes with `/`:** Classes like `bg-accent/15` contain a `/` which is valid in Tailwind but causes issues with `classList.toggle()`. The workaround is to use `el.className` replacement or to pre-define these as the full template string in `renderSidebar()` (which re-renders every 2s anyway, so toggle-based updates are unnecessary). Since `renderSidebar()` already re-renders on every poll cycle, `setFilter()` only needs to toggle `hidden` on run cards -- the visual state will be corrected on the next 2s tick.

Simplified `setFilter()`:
```js
function setFilter(f) {
  activeFilter = f;
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-path]').forEach(c => {
    c.hidden = f !== 'all' && c.dataset.status !== f;
  });
  renderSidebar(); // forces re-render with correct active states
}
```

#### 6.3 `selectRun()` — simpler with re-render

